From 093c70521eeede4669390c9ce66163b4dd7a420e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sss <sss@dark-alexandr.net>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:23:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Remap generation stop from Escape to Ctrl+Escape

Plain Escape no longer aborts AI response generation: it only cancels/
saves an active message edit (with stopImmediatePropagation so it does
not cascade into panel-closing handlers).

Stopping generation is now a last-resort fallback at the end of the
Ctrl+Escape chain in RossAscends-mods.js, fired only when no popup or
legacy panel is open and #mes_stop is visible, preserving the original
swipe-left logic afterwards.

Update help_hotkeys_15 in ru/fr/zh locales to match hotkeys.html docs
(Ctrl+Escape = stop generation).
---
